how metal was that eddie munson moment  in the stranger things season four  finale and why was it the perfect choice  for the character keep watching as we  break it all down  stranger things fans have had a  painstakingly long wait for the final  feature-length episodes of season four  after volume 1 arrived on may 27th but  netflix has finally released the last  two chapters and they drastically  changed the future of the hit series  while the end of volume 1 revealed that  the terrifying villain becna is not only  henry creel but also one volume 2 mainly  revolves around the gang's attempt to  kill him by using max's bait after all  he's already had a taste of her pain and  he wants to finish the job this is  partly because vechna's master plan  involves ripping open four gates across  hawkins using four deaths as a way of  bridging the real world with the upside  down mistakes have never been higher and  there's been talk of a tragic death in  the series since before this season  started so it's a little nerve-wracking  when steve nancy and robin all lie and  wait for becknet at the creel house  while dustin and eddie keep the demo  bats distracted with an impromptu metal  concert at the trailer park  unfortunately the battle comes at high  price for eddie the leader of the  hellfire club has been a big focus this  season since the hawkins townsfolk think  he's responsible for the deaths of  chrissy fred and patrick it's all down  to the very real satanic panic that  gripped the united states in the 1980s  which led many to believe that dungeons  and dragons was part of some sinister  evil plot to corrupt young people  these murders are ritualistic sacrifices  although eddie spends most of his time  hiding and going on the run he armors up  to help steve nancy robin and dustin in  the upside down eddie's idea of  distracting the demo bats is a pretty  inspired one he grabs the upside down  version of his electric guitar and  climbs on top of the trailer to  absolutely shred metallica's master of  puppets as a siren song to draw the demo  bats away from the kreel house it's an  act that fits his character perfectly  since he's a metal head as well as the  dungeon master it's a pretty appropriate  song choice too since vechna is also a  master of the upside down the scene  allows eddie to let loose for a few  minutes after spending days hiding in  the woods by lover's leg he just gets  lost in the music knowing that it's  helping in the fight against vecna are  you ready for the most metal concert in  the history of the world eddie's  performance is another example of how  powerful music can be in the series  after all kate bush is running up that  hill is max's hopeful anthem to pull  herself out of the upside down in  episode four but eddie putting himself  on the line shows he's grown up a bit  unfortunately eddie and dustin's plan  works a little too well and they have to  deal with a huge swarm of demo bats that  assault the trailer eventually breaking  in through the vents the beasts are  small but they're vicious dustin climbs  through the gate back into the real  world but eddie severs the makeshift  sheetrobe so that he can't come back  through and get hurt obviously this  leaves eddie trapped in the upside down  it's a selfless act of heroism and it  proves that eddie isn't afraid to grow  up and take responsibility for his own  actions although at first it looks like  eddie might get away from the demo bats  on a bike one of them knocks it out from  underneath him and he's suddenly swarmed  by the monsters choosing to save dustin  while drawing the demo bats away from  his young sidekick in the creel house  proves that eddie has grown up since the  start of the season when he jokes about  being held back at high school and  refusing to conform with society  although dustin gets back through the  gate to find his friend he's too late  and in a heartbreaking goodbye eddie  passes the mantle of dungeon master onto  him noting that he didn't run away this  time fans have been worried about  eddie's fate for a while and this loss  definitely hurts considering how  charismatic joseph quinn was in the role  but at least it had meaning  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  stranger things season 4 coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one
 

